## Introduction

This is the dataset of DFT-SCAN+rVV10 data in CeO$_2$-ZrO$_2$ ceramics for training DeepMD model. Type 1, 2, and 3 are O, Zr, and Ce respectively. The users can refer to Ref. [1] for details. An example of INCAR is shown in Supplementary Material of Ref. [1].

## General Approach

The DFT dataset was prepared using "dpgen simplify" implemented in DP-GEN (Deep Generator) [2]. 1,968 representative structures were picked up from the structures in the relevant DFT-PBEsol dataset (dataset CeO2-ZrO2-PBEsol from Ref. [3]).

In the labeling phase, the energy, atomic forces, and stresses of the chosen configurations were computed using the Vienna ab initio simulation package (VASP) [4,5], employing the SCAN+rVV10 functional [6]. The calculations were set with a plane-wave cutoff of 1200 eV and a 3×3×3 Monkhorst-Pack k-mesh to ensure convergence of the energies, atomic forces, and virials for the distorted crystals and liquid configurations of CeO$_2$-ZrO$_2$ systems. To accelerate the DFT calculations, a sequential two-step strategy is implemented. In the first step, wavefunctions of electrons are brought to a preliminary level of convergence rapidly with reduced precision, facilitated by enabling specific computational efficiency settings in VASP (see Supplementary Materials in Ref. [1] for details). Following this, the calculation is advanced to a high precision, commencing from the initially preconverged wavefunctions. This approach effectively reduces the overall computational time while maintaining  accuracy of the results.

